Enable the single-threaded sigprocmask() path on wasm.

Upstream omits mythread_sigmask() when __wasm__ is defined, assuming a WASI
target with no POSIX signals, but signals.c still calls it unconditionally and
fails to compile. This wasm32-unknown-linux-musl target has an ordinary musl
with sigprocmask(), so take the single-threaded signal-mask path.

diff --git a/src/common/mythread.h b/src/common/mythread.h
index 10ea2d4..8787cc4 100644
--- a/src/common/mythread.h
+++ b/src/common/mythread.h
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ do { \
 } while (0)
 
 
-#if !(defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__CYGWIN__)) && !defined(__wasm__)
+#if !(defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__CYGWIN__))
 // Use sigprocmask() to set the signal mask in single-threaded programs.
 #include <signal.h>
 
